# UI styling

> Purpose: one shared, Tailwind-based component system for every surface. Extend it; never replace it.

## Rules

### Stack & tokens
1. **Tailwind CSS** is the only styling engine. Theme via `tailwind.config` / `@theme`: colors (primary, surface, border, muted, danger, success), `fontSize`, spacing, radius, shadow, maxWidth, z-index scale (`ui-components.mdc`). No raw hex in markup; `@apply` only inside shared component files.
2. **Look & feel** (palette, type, mood) comes from the approved direction in `design-direction.mdc` → `frontend-design/SKILL.md`. **Layout** comes from `layout-strategy.mdc` → `route-layouts.mdc`.
3. **Extend, don't replace:** add theme keys, marketing gradients, and `components/ui/*` variants that compose the primitives. Per-usage tweaks go in `className` overrides on the catalog component, specified in the content (`ui-components.mdc` §1b).
4. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and `prefers-color-scheme`. Dark mode mirrors tokens — no un-themed surfaces.

### UX principles
| Principle | Apply |
|-----------|-------|
| Simplify | One primary job per screen; remove what does not serve it |
| Hierarchy | Title → supporting text → one main CTA |
| Consistency | Same pattern for nav, forms, cards, empty states |
| Clarity | Plain language; visible labels; icon-only needs `aria-label`/tooltip |
| Feedback | Loading, success, error, empty — always visible |
| Flow | Short paths; back/escape always available |
| Touch | Targets ≥ ~44px; spacing prevents mis-taps |
| Accessible | Contrast, focus ring, keyboard, semantic landmarks, one H1 per view |

### Layout primitives
| Primitive | Rule |
|-----------|------|
| Grid / Flex / Gap | `grid` for dashboards/cards/galleries, `flex` for rows/toolbars; `gap-*` over margins |
| Spacing | Scale only (`p-*`, `m-*`); consistent page padding; 4/8px rhythm |
| Position | z-index from theme scale; `sticky top-*` for headers/table heads via a header-height token |
| Page shell | Max-width container + safe areas; every new page reuses it |
| Sections | Vertical rhythm; optional subtle band |

Layout *strategy* (normal / layout / auto), breakpoints, and per-route layouts: `layout-strategy.mdc`, `route-layouts.mdc`. Folder, shell, and route-folder structure per surface: `project-structure.mdc`. Under Layout Responsive, shells switch by breakpoint (`MobileShell` / `TabletShell` / `DesktopShell`) over one feature tree; tokens, forms, and components are shared.

### Typography
Theme scale only (`text-xs`…`text-4xl+`); `h1`–`h6` map to the display scale; body `text-base leading-relaxed`; muted via token; links use brand color + underline-offset on hover; labels `text-sm font-medium`.

### Shared components
Every component (button, alert, forms, picker, modal, popover, slides, card, navbar, tabs, loader, list, chart, …) follows the catalog and Component Spec in `ui-components.mdc` and lives in `components/ui/<group>/`. Behaviors that apply everywhere: Button never double-submits; Alert is never `window.alert`; Modal traps focus and closes on Esc; skeletons for content, spinners only for tiny contexts; charts use theme colors and a table fallback.

### Motion & scroll
- Page and element transitions (push/pop, sheets, fades, gestures, tokens, reduced motion): `transitions.mdc`
- Infinite scroll: intersection sentinel + skeleton rows, dedupe requests, inline error + retry, "Load more" fallback for a11y, keep scroll on back-nav
- Slideshow/carousel: arrows, dots, swipe, keyboard; autoplay off or reduced-motion safe; lazy off-screen slides
- Parallax / glass / scroll reveal: **marketing only**, subtle, disabled under reduced motion; never on forms, dashboards, or tables
- Micro-interactions on the primary CTA only; budget 2–3 intentional motions per landing page

### Frontend conventions
- Semantic HTML; visible focus; lazy-loaded routes/chunks; one baseline route owns the visual language
- API base URL comes from env (`VITE_*` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` / `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` or equivalent) — never hardcoded; when the backend is separate it also lives in GitHub Secrets (`/deploy`)

## Do not
- Inline styles for colors/spacing that bypass tokens (rare dynamic values excepted)
- Remove focus rings or back affordances for aesthetics
- Add a second spacing or type scale outside the Tailwind theme
- Replace Button/Modal/Form primitives with ad-hoc copies
